lsof -ti:8001 | xargs <span class="hljs-built_in">kill</span> -9
</code></pre><!----></div></div></div><!----><!----><!----></code-block><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></response-element><hr data-path-to-node="7"><h3 data-path-to-node="8">Step 2: The "Room Shift" (Moving to 8002)</h3><p data-path-to-node="9">If Port 8001 is being particularly stubborn (sometimes Android locks ports for several minutes), the easiest way to get SAGE‚Äôs eyes back online is to just move the whole operation to <b data-path-to-node="9" data-index-in-node="183">Port 8002</b>.</p><p data-path-to-node="10">I have updated the logic below to handle the port move for both the <b data-path-to-node="10" data-index-in-node="68">Brain</b> and the <b data-path-to-node="10" data-index-in-node="82">Mirror</b>.</p><p data-path-to-node="11"><b data-path-to-node="11" data-index-in-node="0">Run this to remap SAGE to Port 8002:</b></p><response-element class="" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><code-block _nghost-ng-c803817860="" class="ng-tns-c803817860-420 ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="code-block ng-tns-c803817860-420 ng-animate-disabled ng-trigger ng-trigger-codeBlockRevealAnimation" jslog="223238;track:impression,attention;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_530d0087ec43270c&quot;,&quot;c_13f9c342beb7b685&quot;,null,&quot;rc_f0798b9cae698b93&quot;,null,null,&quot;en&quot;,null,1,null,null,1,1]]" data-hveid="0" decode-data-ved="1" data-ved="0CAAQhtANahgKEwjTtfHboPeTAxUAAAAAHQAAAAAQrwI" style="display: block;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="code-block-decoration header-formatted gds-title-s ng-tns-c803817860-420 ng-star-inserted" style=""><span _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="ng-tns-c803817860-420">Bash</span><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="buttons ng-tns-c803817860-420 ng-star-inserted"><!----><button _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" aria-label="Copy code" mat-icon-button="" mattooltip="Copy code" class="mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger copy-button ng-tns-c803817860-420 mat-unthemed _mat-animation-noopable ng-star-inserted" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" mat-ripple-loader-centered="" jslog="179062;track:generic_click,impression;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_530d0087ec43270c&quot;,&quot;c_13f9c342beb7b685&quot;,null,&quot;rc_f0798b9cae698b93&quot;,null,null,&quot;en&quot;,null,1,null,null,1,1]];mutable:true"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-icon-button__ripple"></span><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" role="img" fonticon="content_copy" class="mat-icon notranslate gds-icon-s google-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="content_copy"></mat-icon><!----><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button><!----><!----></div><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="formatted-code-block-internal-container ng-tns-c803817860-420"><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="animated-opacity ng-tns-c803817860-420"><pre _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="ng-tns-c803817860-420"><code _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" role="text" data-test-id="code-content" class="code-container formatted ng-tns-c803817860-420"><span class="hljs-comment"># 1. Update the files to use 8002 instead of 8001</span>
sed -i <span class="hljs-string">'s/8001/8002/g'</span> ~/sage/*.py
sed -i <span class="hljs-string">'s/8001/8002/g'</span> ~/sage/*.sh
sed -i <span class="hljs-string">'s/8001/8002/g'</span> ~/sage/*.html

<span class="hljs-comment"># 2. Restart the Brain on the new port</span>
python ~/sage/server.py
</code></pre><!----></div></div></div><!----><!----><!----></code-block><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></response-element><hr data-path-to-node="13"><h3 data-path-to-node="14">Step 3: Sync the Mirror</h3><p data-path-to-node="15">Once you see <b data-path-to-node="15" data-index-in-node="13">"SAGE SYSTEM: ONLINE (Port 8002)"</b> in your terminal:</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="16"><li><p data-path-to-node="16,0,0">Go back to your browser.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="16,1,0">The Mirror UI should still be at <code data-path-to-node="16,1,0" data-index-in-node="33">http://localhost:8080/mirror.html</code>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="16,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="16,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Refresh the page.</b> The script inside will now automatically look for the Brain on <b data-path-to-node="16,2,0" data-index-in-node="81">8002</b>.</p></li></ol><h3 data-path-to-node="17">Why this fixes the Handshake:</h3><p data-path-to-node="18">When the port is "already in use," the server doesn't actually start, which is why the Mirror stays stuck on "Awaiting Handshake." By shifting to 8002, we give SAGE a clean, empty room to start her broadcast.</p><p data-path-to-node="19"><b data-path-to-node="19" data-index-in-node="0">Once you run the server on 8002, does the Mirror finally flip to green "CONNECTED"?</b></p></div></message-content><!----></div></structured-content-container><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" class="response-footer complete has-thoughts is-mobile gap"><!----><!---->