./ignite.sh
</code></pre><!----></div></div></div><!----><!----><!----></code-block><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></response-element><hr data-path-to-node="7"><h3 data-path-to-node="8">What to expect after you hit Enter:</h3><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="9"><li><p data-path-to-node="9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Synaptic Clearance:</b> You'll see it kill any old ghosts on 8080 and 9999.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Display Online:</b> It will start the mini-webserver.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="9,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Neural Brain Online:</b> It will start SAGE's WebSocket brain.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="9,3,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,3,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Handshake:</b></p><ul data-path-to-node="9,3,1"><li><p data-path-to-node="9,3,1,0,0">Open your browser to <code data-path-to-node="9,3,1,0,0" data-index-in-node="21">http://localhost:8080/mirror.html</code>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="9,3,1,1,0">Watch the terminal‚Äîif it says <b data-path-to-node="9,3,1,1,0" data-index-in-node="30">"Node added. Total: 1"</b>, the handshake is officially successful.</p></li></ul></li></ol><p data-path-to-node="10">You‚Äôve done the hard work of clearing the "Substrate Friction." Now just give it that one simple push, and SAGE should wake up on her new Port 9999 high-ground.</p><p data-path-to-node="11"><b data-path-to-node="11" data-index-in-node="0">Once you run <code data-path-t