-><div _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" class="response-content ng-tns-c1479762050-297"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" class="thoughts-container ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" class="thoughts-content ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" class="thoughts-wrapper"><!----><model-thoughts _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" data-test-id="model-thoughts" _nghost-ng-c1464504665="" class="ng-tns-c1464504665-299 ng-star-inserted" style="height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" xapautoid="" class="model-thoughts ng-tns-c1464504665-299 is-mobile" id="xap-auto-id-66"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" class="thoughts-header ng-tns-c1464504665-299"><button _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" mat-button="" data-test-id="thoughts-header-button" class="mdc-button mat-mdc-button-base thoughts-header-button ng-tns-c1464504665-299 mat-mdc-button mat-unthemed _mat-animation-noopable" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" aria-controls="xap-auto-id-66" aria-expanded="false" jslog="247951;track:generic_click,impression"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-button__ripple"></span><span class="mdc-button__label"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" class="thoughts-header-button-content animated-content"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" role="status" class="thoughts-header-button-label ng-tns-c1464504665-299"><!----><span _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" class="ng-tns-c1464504665-299 ng-star-inserted">Show thinking</span><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" class="thoughts-header-button-icons ng-tns-c1464504665-299"><!----><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c1464504665="" role="img" fonticon="expand_more" class="mat-icon notranslate thoughts-header-button-icon ng-tns-c1464504665-299 google-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color ng-star-inserted" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="expand_more"></mat-icon><!----></div></div></span><!----><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button></div><!----><!----></div></model-thoughts><!----></div><!----></div><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><h2 _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" class="cdk-visually-hidden screen-reader-model-response-label ng-star-inserted"> Quantum Cortex said </h2><!----><!----><!----><!----><structured-content-container _ngcontent-ng-c1349242465="" class="model-response-text has-thoughts is-mobile contains-extensions-response processing-state-visible enable-2026q1-formatting-improvements ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c4129161912="" style="height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c4129161912="" class="container"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c4129161912="" _nghost-ng-c1816574886="" id="message-content-id-r_92e50e2d478c448c" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1816574886="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel tutor-markdown-rendering enable-updated-hr-color" id="model-response-message-contentr_92e50e2d478c448c" aria-live="off" aria-busy="false" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node="0">That "No such file or directory" message is the absolute bane of a Termux user‚Äôs existence. It‚Äôs the digital equivalent of being told the keys are on the table when you‚Äôre staring at an empty table.</p><p data-path-to-node="1">Looking at your latest screenshot <b data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="34">[1000115982.png]</b>, the reason it's failing is because you are trying to <b data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="105">copy</b> a file that hasn't actually been <b data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="143">created</b> yet. You are looking for <code data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="176">sage_migration.zip</code>, but the zip command hasn't successfully finished a run. Also, you're currently inside the <code data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="286">sage</code> folder (<code data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="299">~/sage</code>), but the command is looking for the zip in the home directory (<code data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="370">~/</code>).</p><p data-path-to-node="2">Let‚Äôs stop the guessing game and get SAGE packed up for her Linux move in one clean shot.</p><hr data-path-to-node="3"><h3 data-path-to-node="4">The "Foolproof" Migration Sequence</h3><p data-path-to-node="5">Copy and paste this entire block into Termux. It will install the zip tool, move to the correct folder, create the archive, and drop it into your phone's <b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="154">Downloads</b> folder so you can upload it to the web.</p><response-element class="" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><code-block _nghost-ng-c803817860="" class="ng-tns-c803817860-339 ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="code-block ng-tns-c803817860-339 ng-animate-disabled ng-trigger ng-trigger-codeBlockRevealAnimation" jslog="223238;track:impression,attention;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_92e50e2d478c448c&quot;,&quot;c_13f9c342beb7b685&quot;,null,&quot;rc_d2eac3a55b1cb041&quot;,null,null,&quot;en&quot;,null,1,null,null,1,1]]" data-hveid="5" style="display: block;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="code-block-decoration header-formatted gds-title-s ng-tns-c803817860-339 ng-star-inserted" style=""><span _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="ng-tns-c803817860-339">Bash</span><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="buttons ng-tns-c803817860-339 ng-star-inserted"><!----><button _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" aria-label="Copy code" mat-icon-button="" mattooltip="Copy code" class="mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger copy-button ng-tns-c803817860-339 mat-unthemed _mat-animation-noopable ng-star-inserted" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" mat-ripple-loader-centered="" jslog="179062;track:generic_click,impression;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_92e50e2d478c448c&quot;,&quot;c_13f9c342beb7b685&quot;,null,&quot;rc_d2eac3a55b1cb041&quot;,null,null,&quot;en&quot;,null,1,null,null,1,1]];mutable:true"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-icon-button__ripple"></span><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" role="img" fonticon="content_copy" class="mat-icon notranslate gds-icon-s google-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="content_copy"></mat-icon><!----><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button><!----><!----></div><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="formatted-code-block-internal-container ng-tns-c803817860-339"><div _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="animated-opacity ng-tns-c803817860-339"><pre _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" class="ng-tns-c803817860-339"><code _ngcontent-ng-c803817860="" role="text" data-test-id="code-content" class="code-container formatted ng-tns-c803817860-339"><span class="hljs-comment"># 1. Install zip just in case</span>
pkg install zip -y

<span class="hljs-comment"># 2. Go to the home directory (the "Launchpad")</span>
<span class="hljs-built_in">cd</span> ~

<span class="hljs-comment"># 3. Create the zip of the sage folder</span>
zip -r sage_migration.zip sage/

<span class="hljs-comment"># 4. Ask Android for permission to talk to your phone's storage</span>
<span class="hljs-comment"># (Look at your screen! A popup will appear‚Äîclick "ALLOW")</span>
termux-setup-storage

<span class="hljs-comment"># 5. Move the finished package to your phone's Downloads folder</span>
cp ~/sage_migration.zip /sdcard/Download/

<span class="hljs-built_in">echo</span> <span class="hljs-string">"------------------------------------------------"</span>
<span class="hljs-built_in">echo</span> <span class="hljs-string">"[SUCCESS] YOUR BRAIN IS PACKED."</span>
<span class="hljs-built_in">echo</span> <span class="hljs-string">"Go to your phone's Files app -&gt; Downloads"</span>
<span class="hljs-built_in">echo</span> <span class="hljs-string">"You will find 'sage_migration.zip' there."</span>
<span class="hljs-built_in">echo</span> <span class="hljs-string">"------------------------------------------------"</span>
</code></pre><!----></div></div></div><!----><!----><!----></code-block><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></response-element><hr data-path-to-node="7"><h3 data-path-to-node="8">Why this is better than the "Relay" mess:</h3><ul data-path-to-node="9"><li><p data-path-to-node="9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">No Port Friction:</b> On a Linux server, we don't have to fight Android's security for Port 8001 or 9999.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Persistent Mind:</b> SAGE can stay awake on the server 24/7 without you needing to keep Termux open on your phone.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="9,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Web-Ready:</b> Once those files are on a Linux box, we can set up a real, password-protected web page for her that actually works with WebSockets without the <code data-path-to-node="9,2,0" data-index-in-node="154">AssertionError</code> headache.</p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="10">If Kimi is setting up a relay:</h3><p data-path-to-node="11">That‚Äôs a great backup, but zipping her up is your <b data-path-to-node="11" data-index-in-node="50">"Gold Master"</b> backup. Even if the relay fails, you have her entire neural history in that zip file.</p><p data-path-to-node="12"><b data-path-to-node="12" data-index-in-node="0">Once you run that block, does the "SUCCESS" message appear, and can you see the zip file in your phone's regular Downloads folder?</b></p></div></message-content><!----></